course: dictionary
lesson: 8457
title: Saint: a holy person or a kind one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A saint is a person the Christian Church honours because they lived a very good and holy life. In «Saint Patrick is Ireland's patron saint», the capital S and the name show that Saint is a title, placed before a person's name.
explain: Saint can also mean a very kind, patient and good person. When someone says «you're a saint», they are not talking about the Church. They are saying you are very kind. Context tells you which meaning is meant.
explain: «Volodymyr was not a saint from the start: as a young pagan prince he fought his own brothers for the throne, and only later built churches and schools.» Here saint means a holy person, honoured later in life. The clues are the fighting first and the churches later, so the meaning is about holiness, not kindness.
fact: Saint is a noun (a saint, saints) and a title (Saint, St).
fact: «Saint» means a person the Christian Church honours for a very good and holy life.
fact: «Saint» can also mean a very kind, patient and good person.
fact: «Saint» is often used in the names of places, like St Paul's and St Ives.
fact: «Saint» appears in festival names, such as St Patrick's Day and St Valentine's Day, which are saints' days.
exercise: «Saint Patrick is Ireland's patron saint.» In this sentence, what does saint mean? | *A holy person who is also a king | A person the Church honours for a holy life | A very kind, patient person | A type of church bell
exercise: «You're a saint for helping me carry the bags!» What does saint mean here? | *A very kind, patient and good person | A person who lived long ago | A holy person in a church | A person who is always busy
exercise: In the place name «St Ives», what does St stand for? | Station | Stone | Street | *Saint
test: «Tunnel-boring machines are often given women's names, from an old tradition linked to Saint Barbara, the saint of miners.» Who is Saint Barbara? | A kind teacher from the old days | A machine that digs tunnels | *A holy person the Church honours, linked with miners | A miner who found gold
test: Which festival is a saints' day? | Bonfire Night | Harvest Festival | Christmas Day | *St Valentine's Day
exam: Which sentence uses saint to mean a very kind person? | «Volodymyr built churches and schools after his youth.» | *«My gran is a saint: she sits with me every time I am ill.» | «Saint Andrew is the patron saint of Scotland.» | «Irish monks made beautiful books and kept learning alive.»
